<http://data.silknow.org/event/2266a099-ec16-312b-9b4a-cd7c9f4d2022>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Purchased from Susan Cowdy (nee Stewart Liberty, 1914-1996), who stated that the hat and dresses were worn 'by a member of the Liberty family'. Susan Cowdy's mother was Evelyn Katherine Phipps (1889-1966), so these pieces from the 1890s are possibly worn by her mother, Ada Rebecca Liberty (1853-1933). \n\nSusan Cowdy's address was 'Swyllmers', The Lee, Great Missenden, Buckinghamshire."@en ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/673542e6-e634-3c22-8b05-ff8f07e61024> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Purchased from Susan Cowdy (nee Stewart Liberty, 1914-1996), who stated that the hat and dresses were worn 'by a member of the Liberty family'. Susan Cowdy's mother was Evelyn Katherine Phipps (1889-1966), so these pieces from the 1890s are possibly worn by her mother, Ada Rebecca Liberty (1853-1933). \n\nSusan Cowdy's address was 'Swyllmers', The Lee, Great Missenden, Buckinghamshire."@en .

